file: "packages/editor/src/canvas/canvas.tsx"
doc: "The single SVG scene and its navigation and selection gestures."

structs: [
  { name: "CanvasProps"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Gains `onContextMenu`, called when the user right-clicks the canvas,\n"
      "with the client point of the press. Every other field is unchanged\n"
      "and is restated because a MODIFIED struct declares its whole shape.\n"
      "\n"
      "REQUIRED, not optional, and for the reason the two optional props\n"
      "beside it are a cautionary tale rather than a precedent. An optional\n"
      "prop is a promise that some construction site populates it, and\n"
      "nothing checks that one does: `focus-inspector` resolved its chord\n"
      "and called `undefined?.()` for months because CommandContext's field\n"
      "was optional and the single construction site never wired it. There\n"
      "is exactly one caller here, so requiring it costs nothing, and the\n"
      "failure if it were optional and app.tsx's node landed without the\n"
      "wiring is that right-click silently does nothing forever. A required\n"
      "prop makes that a compile error. registerCommandContext above was\n"
      "made required on the same argument.\n"
      "\n"
      "The canvas does not own the menu, render it, or know what is on it --\n"
      "it reports a gesture and the shell decides. That keeps the menu a\n"
      "sibling of the overlays in app.tsx rather than something inside the\n"
      "SVG, which is the same split CommandPalette already has."
    fields: [
      { name: "diagram",                type: { named: { symbol: "Diagram" } } },
      { name: "layoutEngine",           type: { named: { symbol: "LayoutEngine" } } },
      { name: "scene",                  type: { named: { symbol: "Scene" } } },
      { name: "stylesheet",             type: { named: { symbol: "Stylesheet" } } },
      { name: "theme",                  type: { named: { symbol: "Theme" } } },
      { name: "ui",                     type: { named: { symbol: "UiState" } } },
      { name: "state",                  type: { named: { symbol: "EditorState" } } },
      { name: "onFocusInspector",       type: { arrow: { output: { primitive: VOID } } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "onSave",                 type: { arrow: { output: { primitive: VOID } } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "registerCommandContext", type: { arrow: { inputs: [ { arrow: { output: { named: { symbol: "CommandContext" } } } } ], output: { primitive: VOID } } } },
      { name: "onContextMenu",          type: { arrow: { inputs: [{ named: { symbol: "Vec2" } }], output: { primitive: VOID } } } }
    ]
    typescript: { struct_kind: STRUCT_KIND_INTERFACE }
  }
]

constants: [
  { name: "Canvas"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Two additions. Everything else -- the pan/zoom group, the three\n"
      "layers, the wheel handler, the keydown listener, the text editor,\n"
      "fit-on-load, the modal-gesture preview and dimming -- is untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "1. onPointerDown RETURNS EARLY when event.button is 2, before it\n"
      "   touches anything else.\n"
      "\n"
      "   This is not defensive. pointerdown fires BEFORE contextmenu for a\n"
      "   right-click, and onPointerDown is currently unconditional: it\n"
      "   preventDefaults, setPointerCaptures and routes the press. routePress\n"
      "   special-cases only button 1, so button 2 falls through to the\n"
      "   marquee, move and resize branches. Without this guard a right-click\n"
      "   on empty canvas starts a marquee and clears the selection, and a\n"
      "   right-click on a node captures the pointer and arms a move session\n"
      "   that the right-button pointerup commits as a position edit --\n"
      "   underneath the menu that is opening.\n"
      "\n"
      "   Return before `props.ui.setModalGesture(undefined)` too. A press is\n"
      "   not a command dispatch, and cancelling a modal gesture because the\n"
      "   user opened a menu is a surprise; the menu closes on Escape and\n"
      "   leaves the gesture alone.\n"
      "\n"
      "2. A `contextmenu` listener on the container element, doing three\n"
      "   things in this order:\n"
      "     a. preventDefault, so the browser menu does not appear. Nothing\n"
      "        handles right-click today, so that native menu is what a user\n"
      "        gets over the canvas now.\n"
      "     b. Build a PressContext with button 2 and the hit under the\n"
      "        pointer, call routePress, and apply the `selection` it returns.\n"
      "        The selection rule lives THERE, not here -- routePress already\n"
      "        decides what a press selects, and a second copy in this\n"
      "        component is a second thing to keep in step.\n"
      "     c. Call props.onContextMenu with the event\'s clientX/clientY.\n"
      "\n"
      "   Widen the file-local `hitAt` helper to take a MouseEvent rather than\n"
      "   a PointerEvent. A contextmenu event is a MouseEvent, PointerEvent\n"
      "   extends MouseEvent, and hitAt only reads clientX/clientY -- so the\n"
      "   widening is safe and the existing pointer callers are unaffected.\n"
      "\n"
      "   The order in (2) is the whole interaction. The shell builds the\n"
      "   menu\'s rows from the selection, so reporting before selecting gives\n"
      "   a menu for the PREVIOUS selection: right-click a node while another\n"
      "   is selected and you get the other one\'s commands, which then act on\n"
      "   the node you are looking at.\n"
      "\n"
      "The canvas does not own the menu, render it, or know what is on it. It\n"
      "reports a gesture and the shell decides."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Component", args: [{ named: { symbol: "CanvasProps" } }] } }
    uses: ["ElementRef", "routePress", "PressContext"]
  }
]
